    "created_at": "2019-08-20T02:14:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-08-20T02:14:04Z",
    "body": "For the directory module, if the path does not exist, we should continue to display it with an indicator that the path is no longer valid, e.g.\r\n\r\n`/tmp/dummy_dir (deleted)`\r\n\r\nFor modules that rely on scanning `pwd`, it's not so clear how to redirect them in a way that doesn't crash. Perhaps the simplest option would be to make the working directory an `Option`, then follow the compiler errors to refactor other modules.",
