    "body": "If the user has disabled all modules that scan `pwd`, including disabling the \"truncate to repo\" `directory` option, will the `directory` module still open the PWD? Because I don't think there's any need to open it just to do truncation behavior when \"truncate to repo\" is off.\r\n\r\nGiven that, the proposed ` (deleted)` bit should be disableable with a config flag, so users who disable everything else that scans pwd can disable that too and avoid having anything open PWD at all.",
