    "updated_at": "2019-08-20T02:17:53Z",
    "body": "> Perhaps the simplest option would be to make the working directory an `Option`, then follow the compiler errors to refactor other modules.\r\n\r\nI haven't looked at how the code is structured, but if \"working directory\" is a path rather than some sort of structure containing directory metadata, it shouldn't be optional. Just because the path doesn't exist on disk doesn't mean we don't have a path.\r\n\r\nModules in general should be resilient against filesystem errors. For example, what if PWD exists, but querying `$PWD/.git` gives me a permissions error?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
